      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Reject raw strings for enum-valued market fields",
      "description": "`StrEnum` members compare equal to their string values, so the membership check accepts `\"period_start\"` and leaves that plain `str` stored in `Market.source_bar_stamping`. This violates the field\u2019s `TimeMeaning` contract and can break consumers that rely on enum identity. There is a related ordering-dependent validation issue in `_normalize_bases`: it converts inputs to a `frozenset` before checking their types, so `[AdjustmentBasis.RAW, \"raw\"]` can pass while the reversed order fails. Validate element types before relying on equality or deduplicating, and add regression tests for these cases.",
